# ============================================================================
# SanctuaryWorld -- Godot project ignore rules
# ============================================================================
# The repository-root .gitignore is a stock *Python* template. Several of its
# patterns silently swallow ordinary Godot/GDScript files:
#
#   *.bin                    glTF binary buffers -- i.e. every imported 3D model
#   *.html                   HTML5 export shell, and the browser visitor client
#   *.so *.dll *.lib *.pyd   GDExtension native binaries
#   lib/ var/ target/ env/   directory-name collisions with Python packaging
#   parts/ instance/ .cache  (same)
#   test_data/ test_output/  plausible names for fixture worlds
#
# None of those would have produced an error. `git add` would have reported
# success and quietly staged nothing.
#
# Context: the 2026-04 Godot world (SanctuaryWorld + SanctuaryClient -- the orb,
# the visitor clients, the multiplayer server, the privacy gate) was never
# committed to any repository and is permanently lost. Confirmed 2026-08-04:
# `git log --all --diff-filter=A` across every ref shows zero Godot files have
# ever been added to this repo in its entire history. See
# docs/audits/audit_2026-08-01_wiring.md and the 2026-08-01 instance note.
#
# This file exists so the rebuild cannot be lost the same way. It clears every
# inherited pattern for this subtree, then re-adds only what Godot itself
# generates.
#
# RULE: if you are about to add a broad pattern here, don't. Ignore the exact
# generated path instead. Breadth is what cost us the world the first time.
# ============================================================================

# --- 1. Clear every rule inherited from the repository-root .gitignore. ------
!**/*

# --- 2. Re-ignore only Godot's generated / machine-local artifacts. ----------

# Godot 4 import cache, shader cache, editor state. Fully regenerated on open.
.godot/

# Godot 3 legacy import cache (harmless if unused).
.import/

# Export output. Regenerated by the export step; never a source of truth.
/build/
/exports/
/android/

# Export presets can carry keystore passwords and absolute local paths, and
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. Kept out deliberately -- document any export
# settings that matter in README.md instead, so they survive without leaking.
export_presets.cfg

# Compiled translation output. The source .po / .csv stays tracked.
*.translation
